# Crosstalk: how much of the temperature rise of the heated waveguide reaches its neighbour. The pipeline fits its decay with distance.
# Reference: the same mesh solved with a sparse direct solver in SciPy.
title Neighbouring waveguide 15 um away, 2 um buried oxide
grid dx=0.25 dy=0.25
window width=80 ymin=-10 ymax=5
layer si -10 0
layer sio2 0 5
rect si -0.25 0.25 2 2.25
rect tin -1 1 4 4.25
heater h1 xmin=-1 xmax=1 ymin=4 ymax=4.25 power=0.1
probe wg1 xmin=-0.25 xmax=0.25 ymin=2 ymax=2.25
rect si 14.75 15.25 2 2.25
probe wg2 xmin=14.75 xmax=15.25 ymin=2 ymax=2.25
expect response wg1 h1 171.845291 1e-7
expect response wg2 h1 3.19293489 1e-7
expect pi_power wg1 h1 24.2466154 1e-7
expect peak 41.4476817 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 19200
expect hotter wg1 wg2
